{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Shall flocks and cattle be slaughtered for them and suffice for them?</b> How would this suffice to remove their complaints, since they do not ask for meat except in order to test, as it says (Psalms 78:18): וַיְנַסּוּ אֵל בִּלְבָבָם? For there is no doubt that just as they tested in this matter, they will test with foods other than this without end, and you will not remove their free choice, as the Sages, of blessed memory, stated (Berakhot 33a): הַכֹּל בִּידֵי שָׁמַיִם חוּץ מִיִּרְאַת שָׁמָיִם."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:26.500858854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}